                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_307">Lessness or Westwood,
                        Kent. Augustinian abbey of St Thomas the Martyr</orgName><p>At top of fol.
                        2r: 'Hic est liber ecclesie Beate Thome martiris de liesnes. quem qui ei
                        abstulerit aut illi super eo fraudem fecerit nisi eidem ecclesie
                        satisfecerit plene anathema sit maranatha'.</p><p>At bottom of flyleaf, fol.
                        1r: 'Lyesn. pro vita sancti Brandani mutuato a domino priore sancte
                        trinitatis.' MRJ suggests that this was Petrus Londiniensis, who used the
                        life of St Brendan in his De visionibus (Lambeth Palace, MS
                     51).</p></provenance>
